---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
const request = `curl "https://api.barcodenest.com/v1/products/3017620422003" \\\n+  -H "X-API-Key: YOUR_API_KEY"`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Product Data API for UPC & EAN Catalog Enrichment | BarcodeNest" description="Enrich product catalogs with barcode-based JSON data: names, brands, quantities and images where available. Compare API plans from $9.99/month.">
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Product catalog integrations</div><h1>A product data API for barcode-based catalog enrichment.</h1><p class="lede">Look up UPC, EAN and GTIN identifiers in BarcodeNest's product index. Use structured JSON to prefill product records in retail tools, inventory apps, and catalog import workflows.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-signal" href="/pricing/">Compare API plans</a><a class="button" href="/register/">Test your product sample</a></div></div></header>
  <section class="section"><div class="narrow"><h2>Map product fields into your catalog.</h2><p>Responses can include product name, brand, quantity, categories, countries and image URLs. Food records may also include ingredients, allergens and nutrition. Fields vary by source and product; treat optional fields as optional in your application.</p><p>Use canonical GTIN values to join lookup results to your own records. Keep source information alongside imported metadata, and preserve reviewed values when a response is incomplete. BarcodeNest performs identifier lookup; it does not provide a general keyword product search endpoint.</p><CodeBlock label="Product lookup" code={request} language="bash" /><h2>Design imports around predictable limits.</h2><p>The batch endpoint accepts up to 100 barcodes. Each matched Free result consumes one lifetime credit. Each submitted paid batch item consumes one monthly lookup unit. Failed Free lookups do not consume credits. Deduplicate your input before sending a batch and handle rate-limit responses using the documented retry behavior.</p><p>Starter includes 2,000 monthly calls and 300 requests/minute for $9.99/month. Growth includes 5,000 monthly calls and 1,200 requests/minute for $19.99/month. If an import would exceed those allowances, <a href="/contact/">discuss your requirements</a> before purchasing.</p><h2>Evaluate the fields that matter to your business.</h2><p>Test a representative sample with the 250-credit lifetime Free plan. Measure the percentage of matching products and the completeness of required fields separately: finding a name does not guarantee an image or ingredients. Include regional products and variants in your evaluation.</p><p>The index includes food, beauty, pet food, and other packaged products, with uneven coverage across categories and markets. See <a href="/data/">coverage and sources</a>, <a href="/terms/">data-use terms</a>, and the <a href="/docs/errors/">error reference</a> before deciding whether it fits your application.</p><h2>Integrating inventory software?</h2><p>Read the <a href="/barcode-api-for-inventory/">inventory barcode API guide</a> for scanning and receiving workflows, then <a href="/pricing/">compare monthly and annual plans</a>.</p></div></section>
  <section class="cta-band"><div class="container cta-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">From evaluation to integration</div><h2>Choose the allowance your catalog needs.</h2></div><a class="button button-signal" href="/pricing/">Choose your API plan</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
